{
  "id": "COMPOUND:28201 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between N-[10-(13,14-Methylenedioxyphenyl)-7(E),9(Z)-pentadienoyl]-pyrrolidine and Phosphodiesterase 6C, as this compound is identified as a target of multiple entities that ultimately interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C. Specifically, the compound is linked to Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, a protein involved in chromatin modification, and this enzyme is in turn targeted by two different compounds, Loukacinol B and [(2R,3S,3aE,5S,8R,9Z,11R,12aS)-2,5,11-trimethyl-6,12-dioxo-8-prop-1-en-2-yl-1,2,3,5,7,8,11,12a-octahydrocyclopenta[11]annulen-3-yl] acetate. These compounds are all potential inhibitors of Phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating a possible mechanism of action through the modulation of histone modification or through direct interaction with the enzyme. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
